export const NODES_PART_04 = {
  "convergence_arrive": {"id":"convergence_arrive","title":"Everyone arrives with a different evening","time":"18:41","tone":"ensemble","locationId":"pub","cast":["maya","theo","cal","sophie","tabitha"],"speaker":"cal","prose":["By the time you reach the Crown & Anchor function room, separate plans have become one social object. Maya arrives with the green notice folded under her arm. Theo brings his guitar. Cal has the PA on but no music through it. Sophie has arranged the chairs into something that could become either an audience or a meeting. Tabitha stands just inside the door still wearing the old coat, one hand in the pocket with the key.","Nobody has summoned a formal meeting. That matters. They are here because their arrangements overlap: Maya wants the Thursday group not to vanish into a sentence; Theo wants the song to have a first hearing; Sophie wants the substitute room to count for what it genuinely saves; Tabitha wants the key returned without becoming a mascot; Cal would like everyone to decide before he moves the speaker again.","Your earlier conduct is already in the room even when nobody names it."],"lines":[{"speaker":"maya","text":"I’m not asking to reopen the whole building. I’m asking us not to describe the pub as if nothing was lost.","when":{"flags":{"promisedMaya":true}}},{"speaker":"sophie","text":"And I am not asking anybody to lie. I am asking us to use the room I managed to obtain before it becomes worthless at nine.","when":{"flags":{"promisedSophie":true}}},{"speaker":"tabitha","text":"Can we establish one rule? Nobody photographs me holding the historical key like I’m opening a branch of democracy."},{"speaker":"cal","text":"Second rule: if we are having a constitutional convention, can it happen before soundcheck?"}],"actions":[{"id":"conv_begin_maya","label":"Ask Maya to say exactly what she thinks has been lost.","next":"convergence_settle","intent":"Let the affected organiser define the missing terms","effects":{}},{"id":"conv_begin_sophie","label":"Ask Sophie to state exactly what the pub does preserve.","next":"convergence_settle","intent":"Let the institutional actor define the practical achievement","effects":{}},{"id":"conv_begin_tabitha","label":"Ask Tabitha whether she wants the key discussed at all.","next":"convergence_settle","intent":"Treat access as dependent on a person's consent","effects":{"setRelations":{"tabitha":"consulted"}}},{"id":"conv_begin_song","label":"Ask Theo what he actually needs for tonight to feel like it happened.","next":"convergence_settle","intent":"Reduce the problem to a human desired future","effects":{}}]},
  "convergence_settle": {"id":"convergence_settle","title":"Before anyone solves it","time":"18:45","tone":"ensemble","locationId":"pub","cast":["maya","theo","cal","sophie","tabitha"],"speaker":"maya","prose":["There is a temptation, once five people are in one room, to treat the room itself as progress. The actual effect is messier. Sophie offers tea from a stainless-steel jug because it came with the hire. Maya refuses, then takes one thirty seconds later. Theo checks his guitar tuning quietly enough that it does not become a declaration. Tabitha sits on the edge of a table rather than in one of Sophie’s rows. Cal keeps the speaker on a low hum because silence would make the room feel like a hearing.","Nobody’s position is pure. Maya does want the evening rescued; she also wants the council’s wording corrected. Sophie does want a clean report upward; she also spent her afternoon preventing total cancellation. Tabitha dislikes symbolic politics but has brought the one object that could materially alter access. Theo wants a meaningful first hearing but is embarrassed by the possibility of adults taking risks on his behalf. Cal is the closest thing to an optimiser in the room and keeps discovering that the variables are people.","The atmosphere improves once you stop searching for the character who represents the correct side. The problem is not hidden behind them. It exists between their partially legitimate arrangements."],"lines":[{"speaker":"maya","text":"For the avoidance of doubt, I do not want Sophie fired, the pub boycotted or the building stormed."},{"speaker":"sophie","text":"Thank you. I had not budgeted for any of those outcomes."},{"speaker":"tabitha","text":"Could still storm the building recreationally later."},{"speaker":"theo","text":"Please do not make my song the anthem."}],"actions":[{"id":"settle_listen","label":"Let them finish describing their own positions before you offer one.","next":"convergence_accounts","intent":"Reduce premature intervention","effects":{"addMemories":["listened_before_positioning"]}},{"id":"settle_name_overlap","label":"Say out loud that several people have kept part of their promise and still failed to produce the same evening.","next":"convergence_accounts","intent":"Name the arrangement collision without assigning blame","effects":{"addMemories":["named_partial_promises"]}},{"id":"settle_ask_cost","label":"Ask who currently absorbs the inconvenience if everyone accepts the pub solution.","next":"convergence_accounts","intent":"Locate the cost rather than the winner","effects":{"addMemories":["asked_where_cost_lands"]}}]},
  "convergence_accounts": {"id":"convergence_accounts","title":"The terms do not add up","time":"18:49","tone":"ensemble","locationId":"pub","cast":["maya","theo","cal","sophie","tabitha"],"speaker":"theo","prose":["Once everybody stops arguing about whether the pub is good or bad, the incompatibilities become easier to see. The youth group cannot simply use this room under its normal arrangement. The main hall is physically usable but administratively unsupervised. The side key can open a door but cannot create authority. Sophie’s room expires as a useful substitute if nobody uses it. Tabitha’s last bus now turns half eight from a preference into a boundary. Theo’s desired outcome is almost offensively small: play one song in front of the people who helped shape it.","None of those facts produces a correct answer. Together they produce the evening."],"lines":[{"speaker":"maya","text":"The inspection says the main room passed. The kitchen circuit is isolated. There is no order closing the premises.","when":{"information":["main_room_passed","kitchen_fault_isolated"]}},{"speaker":"sophie","text":"Yes. And a passed room without a responsible person is still a room I cannot authorise you to use.","when":{"information":["main_room_passed"]}},{"speaker":"cal","text":"The pub minimum is real, by the way. We either use the room or the council pays for an empty one and everyone gets to be correct in private.","when":{"information":["pub_minimum_spend"]}},{"speaker":"theo","text":"I do not need a revolution. I need three minutes and forty seconds. Four minutes if Maya makes me put the bridge back."},{"speaker":"tabitha","text":"This is how revolutions begin. Somebody says four minutes, then there are tote bags."}],"actions":[{"id":"accounts_preserve_song","label":"Say the song is the smallest thing everyone might be able to preserve.","next":"convergence_commitments","intent":"Define a narrow shared desired future","effects":{"setArrangements":{"performance":"narrowed_to_one_song"}}},{"id":"accounts_preserve_truth","label":"Say the first priority is stopping ‘continuity’ from swallowing the differences.","next":"convergence_commitments","intent":"Prioritise truthful framing over event completion","effects":{"setFlags":{"publicCorrection":true}}},{"id":"accounts_preserve_people","label":"Say nobody should turn Maya or Tabitha into the person who authorises what the institution will not.","next":"convergence_commitments","intent":"Protect people from absorbing institutional risk","effects":{"addMemories":["named_risk_transfer"]}},{"id":"accounts_preserve_pub","label":"Say the pub room should be used for what it can honestly host before it disappears too.","next":"convergence_commitments","intent":"Prioritise partial practical success","effects":{}}]},
  "convergence_commitments": {"id":"convergence_commitments","title":"What you said earlier is still true","time":"18:57","tone":"ensemble","locationId":"pub","cast":["maya","theo","cal","sophie","tabitha"],"speaker":"tabitha","prose":["The discussion becomes more difficult when it touches commitments instead of principles. Principles can be restated until they fit. A promise has an audience and a remembered shape. Maya has already told the youth group there would be some kind of ending. Sophie has already activated a paid substitute room. Theo and Cal have already carried equipment here. Tabitha has already adjusted her route because of the last bus. Your own earlier words, if you made any, are now part of the same structure.","No interface lists these obligations down the side of the screen. They are legible because people behave as if they matter. Maya checks your face before she mentions reporting back. Sophie glances at the empty place where a photograph might be taken. Tabitha checks the time without announcing that she is checking it. These are not penalties waiting to trigger. They are expectations you can keep, renegotiate, disappoint or decide were never reasonable.","Cal points out that the pub room is booked until 21:30 but the youth-access condition becomes tighter at nine. Tabitha’s bus is 21:12. The hall is a two-minute walk away. Time does not create an action-point economy; it makes incompatible social intentions stop being hypothetical."],"lines":[{"speaker":"maya","text":"You said you’d come back to me before anyone declared victory. I’m counting this as ‘back to me’. I am not counting anything as victory.","when":{"flags":{"promisedMaya":true}}},{"speaker":"sophie","text":"You did say a photograph if the room was genuinely used. I’m not cashing that in before we know what ‘used’ means.","when":{"flags":{"promisedSophie":true}}},{"speaker":"tabitha","text":"And yes, I know half eight is still forty-something minutes away. That is not the point. The point is whether plans only become real when the public thing is finished with them.","when":{"flags":{"promisedTabitha":true}}},{"speaker":"cal","text":"I made no promises except to bring the PA, which is why I am currently morally superior."}],"actions":[{"id":"commitments_keep_all","label":"Say you still want to keep every promise you made, even if that means making the solution smaller.","next":"convergence_public","intent":"Try to narrow scope rather than silently discard commitments","effects":{"addMemories":["tried_to_keep_multiple_commitments"]}},{"id":"commitments_renegotiate","label":"Say circumstances have changed and some expectations now need to be renegotiated explicitly.","next":"convergence_public","intent":"Normalise renegotiation as play rather than failure","effects":{"addMemories":["named_need_to_renegotiate"]}},{"id":"commitments_priority","label":"Say the group should decide which promise protects a person and which mainly protects an institution.","next":"convergence_public","intent":"Distinguish human and institutional stakes","effects":{"addMemories":["distinguished_human_institutional_promises"]}}]}
};
